    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0936" n="832" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg832"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France (Marriner) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-12-27T11:00:00+00:00">December 27,
                            1933—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:20 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d620-f1"/>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>578. For the Acting Secretary and Assistant Secretary Moore only from Bullitt.
                    Soviet Commercial Attaché, Paris, handed me last night list obligations in
                    reichsmarks of the S.S.S.R.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d620-f2"/> falling due in the
                    year 1934. He did not give me list of obligations in dollars falling due in
                    Germany for the same period but promised to telegraph to Berlin at once for it.
                    To cable this list in confidential code is impossible without breaking the code
                    since the Soviet Government has the list and Marriner and I have agreed that the
                    best method of transmission is the following:</p>
                <p>[Here follows instruction as to method of transmitting the information to the
                        Department.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d620-f3"/>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>[Bullitt]</item>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d620-f1" n="65" xml:id="d620-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram in two sections.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d620-f2" n="66" xml:id="d620-f2-content">
                <p>Soyuz Sotsialisticheskikh Sovietskikh Respublik.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d620-f3" n="67" xml:id="d620-f3-content">
                <p>The information was duly sent in telegram No. 579, December 28, 11 a.m.
                    (800.51W89 U.S.S.R./20).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
